    "done_when": "A run that crew complete promotes goes from complete straight to promoted in the follower. It never renders \"unpromoted\" in between. Measured on 2026-09-26: roadmap-docstring-names-the-focus-home printed complete → unpromoted at 13:34:04 after crew complete returned ok and its commit was on main, then unpromoted → promoted at 13:34:20. figure-as-text did the same at 15:05. The row lands between the promote commit and the pointer removal. Find where promotion in reckon/crew/promotion.py writes the promote record and removes the live pointer. Make the classification read promoted from the moment the promote record exists, either by ordering or by having the classifier consult that record. Choose the smaller change and say why in the commit. tests/test_a_promotion_never_reads_unpromoted.py drives a synthesised completed run through promotion in tmp_path (the pytest fixture), with every crew directory environment-resolved to tmp_path. It classifies at the instant between writing the promote record and removing the pointer, via a hook or monkeypatch at that boundary, and asserts promoted, not unpromoted. Negative control: the current ordering; the test must fail. The three departure routes named by the section, a refused dispatch, a vanished reflex review and a discard, still never render promoted. Assert one case of each in the same file. tests/test_crew_promotion.py adds no failures against the base, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository. Gate and control logs are written under the run directory. The change is committed in this worktree.",
